---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import SiteNav from '../components/SiteNav.astro';
---
<Base
  title="About San Lee · Technical Program Manager"
  description="San Lee is a technical program management professional with experience across enterprise product delivery, platform engineering, and reliable AI systems."
  canonical="https://sanlee.me/about.html"
  ogType="profile"
>
  <SiteNav current="about" />

  <main class="wrap article-body" id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <a class="back" href="index.html">&larr; Back</a>
    <p class="kicker">About</p>
    <h1>Technical depth, program discipline</h1>
    <p class="subtitle">I work at the seam between product, engineering, and delivery.</p>

    <p class="lead">
      Seven years in infra and operations at the same firm, then a product seat
      on a collaboration platform. I was one person in a large machine. I built
      the public system to own a full loop I did not own at work.
    </p>

    <h2>How I work</h2>
    <p>
      I turn ambiguous goals into sequenced, testable delivery: set the direction,
      make the interfaces between teams and systems explicit, track risks and
      dependencies, and use evidence to decide what ships. When a measurement
      contradicts the plan, I change the plan.
    </p>
    <p>
      For the public system, I set the direction, the contracts, and the bar;
      Claude does most of the typing. The evals and postmortems are the proof,
      including the calls that shipped and the ones the evidence reversed.
    </p>

    <div class="decision">
      <p class="tag">Start with the evidence</p>
      <h2>Selected work</h2>
      <p><a href="projects/the-system.html">AI system architecture and contract testing &rarr;</a></p>
      <p><a href="projects/defense-news-classifier.html">Classifier evaluation and evidence gates &rarr;</a></p>
      <p><a href="projects/product-and-program.html">The system through a TPM lens &rarr;</a></p>
    </div>

    <h2 id="outside">Outside the work</h2>
    <div class="about">
      <p>
        I hike when I can get out, and I take a camera. The frames on this
        site are mine: Jeju&rsquo;s basalt cliffs, lanterns at a temple, a
        trail looking out. The rest lives on
        <a href="https://vsco.co/sanlee">VSCO</a> and in
        <a href="lab/gallery.html">the gallery</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        I speak English and intermediate Korean. Korean is not a skill I
        lead with at work. It is how I get around when I travel there.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sango is a Scottish Fold. He treats the apartment as a post and
        supervises from a nap.
      </p>
      <div class="frame-strip" aria-label="A few frames from the gallery">
        <a class="frame" href="lab/gallery.html">
          <img src="assets/img/photo-pavilion-spring.jpeg" alt="A pavilion over a pond in spring bloom" loading="lazy" width="160" height="160" />
        </a>
        <a class="frame" href="lab/gallery.html">
          <img src="assets/img/photo-jeju.jpeg" alt="Basalt sea cliffs on Jeju Island" loading="lazy" width="160" height="160" />
        </a>
        <a class="frame" href="lab/gallery.html">
          <img src="assets/img/photo-lanterns.jpeg" alt="Lotus lanterns at a temple" loading="lazy" width="160" height="160" />
        </a>
        <a class="frame" href="lab/gallery.html">
          <img src="assets/img/photo-trail.jpeg" alt="A trail overlook in the mountains" loading="lazy" width="160" height="160" />
        </a>
      </div>
      <figure class="sango">
        <img src="assets/img/sango-boop.jpeg" alt="Sango, a Scottish Fold, asleep" loading="lazy" width="240" height="240" />
        <figcaption>Sango, Chief Nap Officer.</figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <p><a href="mailto:hi@sanlee.me">Contact me</a> &middot; <a href="resume.html">View résumé</a></p>
  </main>

  <footer class="footer">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="disclaimer">Personal site &mdash; views and projects are my own, not my employer's.</p>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script is:inline src="/assets/theme.js"></script>
</Base>
